   "synthesis": "- UPSC repeatedly tests **technology distinctions**, not scheme trivia: fuel cell vs combustion; PV vs solar thermal; fission vs fusion vs radioisotope decay; anode vs cathode; gasification feedstock/product chains.\n- Strong trap family = **absolute qualifiers**: “only”, “cannot”, “no pollution”, “always”, “requires 60% enrichment”, “not usable in small devices”.\n- Current events usually act as the wrapper; permanent preparation should retain the underlying mechanism and property statement.\n- UPPCS adds more **direct classification + location/installation recall**; the latter should remain a replaceable current layer."
  },
